{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential","id":1449380,"title":"WoD Crossover potential?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-23T14:39:40-07:00","id":1449380,"title":"WoD Crossover potential?","content":"I know I\u2019ve raised this question before: but I want to ask it again: what do you guys think of a (limited) crossover between two universes, Trinity Continuum and World of Darkness? It\u2019s explicitly mentioned in one of the sourcebooks for Wraith 20, where one of the Doomslayer Wraiths (Alex Corbin) is the ghost of an Inspired aviator who was killed in a plane crash in TC during the Adventure! era. I mean, I know it\u2019s just an Easter egg, but I think it\u2019s a cool idea that Onyx Path should maybe look into developing further.<br /> <br /> Anyway, imma go buy the new False Gods: Ventrue clanbook for CoD. Have a great day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T18:08:20-07:00","id":1449403,"title":"","content":"Mages seem like the best bet, and after them Changelings. All other splats would have their metaphysics truly fouled up. Mages and Changelings could be handled with a different relationship to flux. The Changelings would have to access their powers through dreams and imagination. The Mages would be similar, but far less extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T19:52:03-07:00","id":1449418,"title":"","content":"I've mixed in the Trinity stuff with my City. I had the telluric event occur which caused all the pulp stuff to happen, but then it faded as WW2 came to a close and people slowly forgot it was real, and most of the people became the stuff of pulp novels, tales and legends. For the more modern iteration Aberrant, they are few and far between, with many of shadowy corporations, societies, shadow groups and other things lurking in the cracks, taking an interest in them. For the most part, novas hide, not flaunting their abilities. A few act as costumed vigilantes but the moment they are caught on film, the things in the cracks and shadows come hunting them, and they often don't last long. As we know, the future is the Psi Talents, the Psions. I have them as well, but like the novas, rare as anything, and while they can hide their abilities better, they too are targets of those shadows that hunt them for their own plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T20:27:12-07:00","id":1449419,"title":"","content":"The TC core book states on page 164:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Maxwell </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mercer seemed to have an eye towards the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">strange, and sure enough wherever he direct</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">ed the Society they discovered undead, aliens, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">and any number of other preternatural beings. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mercer always wanted to study and understand, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">but often dangerous creatures have no desire to </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">be studied. So, instead they fought. And often </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">they won.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>So the undead are canon for the Adventure! era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T03:33:47-07:00","id":1449444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential#post1449380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it\u2019s a cool idea that Onyx Path should maybe look into developing further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adventure! is owned by Onyx Path. The WoD is owned by Paradox Interactive. Any crossover between the two is settings extremely unlikely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential?p=1449419#post1449419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The TC core book states on page 164:<br /> <br /> So the undead are canon for the Adventure! era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Phenomena that Adventure!-era science interprets as &quot;undead&quot; are canonical. That's not quite the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T05:28:56-07:00","id":1449449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential?p=1449444#post1449444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Adventure! is owned by Onyx Path. The WoD is owned by Paradox Interactive. Any crossover between the two is settings extremely unlikely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Phenomena that Adventure!-era science interprets as &amp;quot;undead&amp;quot; are canonical. That's not quite the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So stuff like the undead and other supernatural beings have a scientific explanation in the TC. Totally cool. Maybe the TC and the WoD are two different timelines that diverged somewhere in the distant past. Unofficially of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T06:56:49-07:00","id":1449455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential?p=1449449#post1449449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So stuff like the undead and other supernatural beings have a scientific explanation in the TC. Totally cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>For certain values of &quot;scientific&quot;. The cover of TC: Adventure! does show Max Mercer punching a skeleton, and I have no idea how an ambulatory skeleton is supposed to have a &quot;scientific&quot; explanation. The assumption is likely that it is animated by Telluric energy, and no one thinks further on the subject","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T23:54:55-07:00","id":1449620,"title":"","content":"Im making Vampires and Werewolfs as low powered re-fluffed Novas. All the tools are there with the tags (all hail tags!) and transformations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T04:27:13-07:00","id":1449639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential?p=1449455#post1449455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For certain values of &quot;scientific&quot;. The cover of TC: Adventure! does show Max Mercer punching a skeleton, and I have no idea how an ambulatory skeleton is supposed to have a &quot;scientific&quot; explanation. The assumption is likely that it is animated by Telluric energy, and no one thinks further on the subject</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. Adventure-era jargon being interpreted as signs of a etherite-friendly paradigm might be simple and stick quite close to canon, i'd guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T05:26:55-07:00","id":1449646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential?p=1449639#post1449639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This. Adventure-era jargon being interpreted as signs of a etherite-friendly paradigm might be simple and stick quite close to canon, i'd guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:06:28-07:00","id":1450048,"title":"","content":"For a crossover between Mage and Adventure!, I like to replace Dr Hammersmith with Czar Vargo: an Etherite who in the early 20th century attempted a potentially World altering stunts that would have effectively won the Ascension War had he succeeded. Change the method that he used to the same one that Dr Hammersmith used, resulting in a similar outcome: the Inspired Age launched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T15:36:12-07:00","id":1450090,"title":"","content":"My gaming group ran a game years ago that crossed over 1st ed Aberrant, Exalted 2e, and Old WoD (Mage &amp; Werewolf).<br /> It worked fine though there were a number of GM adjustments made, and the Werewolf character ended up being the weakest party member...<br /> <br /> I think a setting hack that introduces Scale to WoD/CoD games would be pretty neat though. Like what if Celerity gave you Speed Scale, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:07:13-07:00","id":1450109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential?p=1450090#post1450090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My gaming group ran a game years ago that crossed over 1st ed Aberrant, Exalted 2e, and Old WoD (Mage &amp; Werewolf).<br /> It worked fine though there were a number of GM adjustments made, and the Werewolf character ended up being the weakest party member...<br /> <br /> I think a setting hack that introduces Scale to WoD/CoD games would be pretty neat though. Like what if Celerity gave you Speed Scale, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, if you're playing WoD you might have to nerf Potence/Celerity/Fortitude a bit. Maybe only increase Scale every third dot, with the 1st, 2nd, 4th, etc. instead providing enhancement.<br /> <br /> As for Werewolves, I think replacing the 6+ Attributes with Scale could work as well (Scale 2 for 6, Scale 2 + 1 or 2 Enhancement for 7, Scale 3 for 8, etc.). That way the Werewolf in their Garou form will almost always provide some combat benefit to the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T19:21:17-07:00","id":1450254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1449380-wod-crossover-potential?p=1450048#post1450048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a crossover between Mage and Adventure!, I like to replace Dr Hammersmith with Czar Vargo: an Etherite who in the early 20th century attempted a potentially World altering stunts that would have effectively won the Ascension War had he succeeded. Change the method that he used to the same one that Dr Hammersmith used, resulting in a similar outcome: the Inspired Age launched.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about that! But I switched Dr. Zorbo with Czar Vargo instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}